GNU diffutils for OpenVMS
=========================

This is GNU diffutils @VERSION@ (cmp, diff, diff3 and sdiff) built natively
for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the unmodified GNU release plus the patches in the
vms-diffutils project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-diffutils

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  diffutils is free software under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later; see COPYING.  The manual is
DIFFUTILS.TXT; CMP.1, DIFF.1, DIFF3.1 and SDIFF.1 are the manual pages.

What is installed
-----------------
    DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[BIN]CMP.EXE, DIFF.EXE, DIFF3.EXE, SDIFF.EXE
    DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[000000]DIFFUTILS$SETUP.COM   defines the commands
    DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[DOC]                         this file, COPYING, NEWS,
                                                 DIFFUTILS.TXT, the manual pages
    SYS$STARTUP:DIFFUTILS$STARTUP.COM            defines DIFFUTILS$ROOT

Setting up
----------
The kit installs DIFFUTILS$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.
To define DIFFUTILS$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line
to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:DIFFUTILS$STARTUP.COM

Each user (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone) then defines the commands:

    $ @DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[000000]DIFFUTILS$SETUP.COM

This defines gdiff (GNU diff), cmp, diff3 and sdiff.  In DCL, DIFF is an
abbreviation of the DIFFERENCES command, so diff itself is defined only on
request:

    $ @DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[000000]DIFFUTILS$SETUP.COM DIFF

after which DIFF runs GNU diff for that user; DIFFERENCES, typed in full,
still runs the VMS command.

Exit status
-----------
Under DCL the status says what happened:

    success     the files are the same
    warning     the files differ (exit code 1): IF .NOT. $STATUS sees it,
                but a command procedure's default ON ERROR does not stop
    error       trouble, such as a missing file (exit code 2)

The exit code N is ($STATUS .AND. %X7F8) / 8.  Under a GNV shell, $? is
the exit code as on Unix.

diff3 and sdiff
---------------
diff3 and sdiff run diff in a subprocess (LIB$SPAWN), with its output in a
temporary file in SYS$SCRATCH.  By default they run
DIFFUTILS$ROOT:[BIN]DIFF.EXE; --diff-program names another.  sdiff -o's
"e" command runs the editor named by the EDITOR logical name or symbol
(default: EDIT) on a temporary file.

Not available on VMS
--------------------
diff -l (--paginate) needs the Unix pr program, which VMS does not have.

Upper-case options and batch jobs
---------------------------------
Under the TRADITIONAL DCL parse style DCL upper-cases the unquoted parts of
a command and the C run-time library passes them to the program in lower
case, so an unquoted -B (ignore blank lines) arrives as -b (ignore changes
in white space) and -U 5 as -u 5.  Batch jobs use TRADITIONAL even when
interactive logins are set to EXTENDED.  Use the long options
(--ignore-blank-lines), quote the short ones ("-B"), or start the
procedure with

    $ SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED
